quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  6,45,"Thus, the (last) remnants of those people who were unjust were cut off. And all praise belongs to Allah, the Lord of all worlds."
  6,46,"Say: ‘What do you think: If Allah takes away your hearing and your sight and seals your hearts, which god besides Allah can bring it (back) to you?’ Look how We explain Our revelations in various ways! Yet they still turn away."
  6,47,"Say: ‘What do you think: If Allah’s punishment comes to you suddenly or openly, would anyone be destroyed except the wrongdoing people?’"
  6,48,"We do not send the messengers except as bearers of glad tidings and as warners. As for those who become believers and righteous, there shall be no fear on them, nor shall they grieve."
  6,49,"But as for those who reject Our Signs, the punishment shall afflict them because of the disobedience they had been committing."
  6,50,"Say (to the disbelievers): ‘I do not say to you that I possess the treasures of Allah, nor do I know the Unseen myself, nor do I say to you that I am an angel. I only follow what is revealed to me.’ Say: ‘Can the blind and the seeing be equal? Will you not then reflect?’"
  6,51,And warn with this (Qur’an) those fearful of being gathered towards their Lord—when they shall have no guardian except Him nor any intercessor; perhaps they may be God-conscious.
  6,52,"Do not drive away those (poor believers) who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking nothing but His countenance (i.e. His nearness and pleasure). Neither are you accountable for them whatsoever, nor are they accountable for you in any way, so that you may turn them away and become among those who deprive others of their rights (and such is not befitting for your compassionate being)."
